      "seed": 600819478,
      "version": 239,
      "versionNonce": 1228233650,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790871646691,
      "created": 1790853658529,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "dbo kyon hota hai? Jab aap SQL Server mein koi naya database\nbanate hain (MyDatabase), toh usme default roop se ek schema banta\nhai jiska naam dbo hota hai. Agar aap table banate waqt koi aur\nschema specify nahi karte, toh wo automatically dbo ke andar save ho\njaati hai (jaise aapki dbo.orders table).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "dbo kyon hota hai? Jab aap SQL Server mein koi naya database banate hain (MyDatabase), toh usme default roop se ek schema banta hai jiska naam dbo hota hai. Agar aap table banate waqt koi aur schema specify nahi karte, toh wo automatically dbo ke andar save ho jaati hai (jaise aapki dbo.orders table).",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
